# Normalize line endings. Text files are stored as LF in the repo and checked
# out as LF on every OS, matching Prettier's default (endOfLine: "lf").
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true produces CRLF working
# files, and `prettier --write` (or `pnpm run format`) rewrites every file back
# to LF — a spurious repo-wide diff that never shows up on the Linux CI box.
# Pinning eol=lf here makes formatting a no-op on a clean checkout everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalize or diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mov  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.pdf  binary

# The review-agent ledger is an append-only log (docs/specs/harness-self-improvement.md §4.1).
# Two branches that both triage a review conflict on its last line every time; union is the
# correct merge for an append-only file — keep both sides' records, drop neither.
review-agents/ledger.jsonl merge=union
